      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "RFC: Claws",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds an RFC for **Claws**: versioned starter setup manifests for OpenClaw agents. A Claw can compose skills, plugins, MCP servers, connectors, workspace files, persona files such as `SOUL.md`, heartbeat/crons, schedules, and automations into one inspectable setup flow.\n\n## Motivation\n\nOpenClaw has skills, plugins, compatible bundles, package sources, and hosted feeds, but not a focused way to describe a governed scenario-level starter setup that can be inspected, dry-run planned, applied, removed, exported, and explained later through provenance.\n\n## Current shape\n\n- Uses `Claw` / `Claws` for the user-facing concept and `claw` for schema/feed/CLI kinds.\n- References RFC 0009 as the feed dependency: feeds provide discovery, curation, approval, block, pin, deprecation, and effective-view resolution.\n- Keeps Claws distinct from packages, plugin-bundled skills, compatible bundles, prior Agent Pack/workspace-template proposals, and whole-agent export/import.\n- States the safety guarantee up front: no silent workspace mutation, no silent automation enablement, and no transitive approval of Claw members.\n- Defines typed entries, `inspect`, dry-run apply plans, consent-gated apply, provenance JSON shapes, workspace-file safety, automation safety, compatibility/migration, creation/export behavior, and acceptance criteria.\n- Aligns with the six authored OpenClaw PRs: validation/dry-run, artifact provenance refs, workspace/persona apply, plugin artifact installers plus uninstall warnings, status/remove lifecycle proof, and creation/export.\n- Adds a four-PR first-series completion track: skill installers, MCP server installers, connector installers, and doctor diagnostics.\n- Adds a separate four-PR automation follow-up track: schema/preview, one consent-gated substrate, provenance/status, and disable/remove E2E.\n- Treats Claw artifact refs as provenance and warning metadata, not uninstall locks. Plugin uninstall warns when Claws reference a plugin, then proceeds when the user confirms or forces it.\n- Does not expose a standalone `claws plan` / `claws feed plan` command in v1; `apply --dry-run --json` emits the non-mutating lifecycle plan.\n- Treats `apply` as the Claw lifecycle verb and `remove` as the Claw-level inverse. Current `remove` clears Claw refs and Claw-managed workspace files; artifact install/uninstall remains underneath for package-like entries.\n- Adds `claws export` as the explicit authoring path for selected local plugins, workspace files, and persona files; it is not whole-instance export/import.\n- Keeps update, automation enablement, disable, and rollback as later lifecycle tracks.\n\n## PR sequencing\n\nAuthored OpenClaw stack:\n\n1. `openclaw/rfcs#27`: RFC and terminology.\n2. `openclaw/openclaw#101328`: non-mutating Claws validation lifecycle.\n3. `openclaw/openclaw#101755`: consent-gated apply and artifact provenance refs.\n4. `openclaw/openclaw#101973`: workspace file and persona apply.\n5. `openclaw/openclaw#102228`: plugin artifact installers and uninstall warnings.\n6. `openclaw/openclaw#102296`: status, remove, and current lifecycle E2E.\n7. `openclaw/openclaw#102306`: creation/export experience.\n\nRemaining first-series OpenClaw track:\n\n1. Skill installers.\n2. MCP server installers.\n3. Connector installers.\n4. Doctor diagnostics.\n\nDependent ClawHub track:\n\n1. Schema ingestion and data model.\n2. Publish validation and authoring docs.\n3. Search, detail, and API surfaces.\n4. Feed export and published E2E.\n\nLater automation track:\n\n1. Automation schema and dry-run preview.\n2. One consent-gated automation substrate.\n3. Automation provenance and status.\n4. Disable/remove and automation E2E.\n\n## Validation\n\nCurrent branch head: `c1d3a8b6e1dcbb11d42da998890de40b49a01b9b`\n\n```text\n$ git diff --check\n# no output\n\n$ rg -n \"ref-count|preexistingDirectInstall|reference accounting|direct-user owner|future mutating|one implementation PR|four-PR OpenClaw\" rfcs/0016-claws.md\n# no output\n```",
        "branch": "capability-packs-rfc",
